# Kotlin Gradle Plugin (KGP) & Built-in Kotlin Migration

## Status (Last Reviewed: 2026-06-21)

| Plugin | Resolved Version | Latest Available | KGP-Free? |
|--------|------------------|------------------|-----------|
| `image_picker_android` | 0.8.13+19 | 0.8.13+19 | ✅ Yes |
| `shared_preferences_android` | 2.4.26 | 2.4.26 | ✅ Yes |
| `url_launcher_android` | 6.3.32 | 6.3.32 | ✅ Yes |
| `package_info_plus` | 10.1.0 | 10.1.0 | ❌ No (upstream) |

## Outcome

After upgrading, `flutter build apk` succeeds. The KGP warning is now reduced from **4 plugins → 1 plugin** (`package_info_plus` only).

```
WARNING: Your app uses the following plugins that apply Kotlin Gradle Plugin (KGP): package_info_plus
Future versions of Flutter will fail to build if your app uses plugins that apply KGP.
```

## Background

Flutter 3.44+ introduced **Built-in Kotlin** support and emits a warning when plugins still apply the Kotlin Gradle Plugin (KGP) via `apply plugin: 'kotlin-android'` or the `id("kotlin-android")` plugin.

> Future versions of Flutter will fail to build if your app uses plugins that apply KGP.

## Investigation Details

### ✅ Flutter team plugins (RESOLVED)

The 3 Flutter-maintained plugins have migrated. Their `android/build.gradle.kts` plugins blocks now contain only `com.android.library` (no more `kotlin-android`):

```kotlin
// image_picker_android 0.8.13+19, shared_preferences_android 2.4.26, url_launcher_android 6.3.32
plugins {
    id("com.android.library")
    // NOTE: "kotlin-android" removed — Built-in Kotlin compatible
}
```

They still carry a `kotlin-gradle-plugin` classpath line, but this is harmless: it is not *applied*, so Flutter's detector no longer flags these plugins.

### ❌ `package_info_plus` 10.1.0 (STILL APPLIES KGP)

This third-party plugin (from `fluttercommunity/plus_plugins`) still uses the old Groovy DSL with an explicit KGP application:

```groovy
// package_info_plus-10.1.0/android/build.gradle
ext.kotlin_version = '2.2.0'
classpath "org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-gradle-plugin:$kotlin_version"
// ...
apply plugin: 'com.android.library'
apply plugin: 'kotlin-android'   // ← This is what triggers the warning
```

This is the **only remaining cause** of the KGP warning. There is no newer version of `package_info_plus` available on pub.dev that resolves it.

