## App-Side Android Config (Already Correct)

The Flutter migrator had already updated the app-side configuration:

**`android/gradle.properties`**:
```properties
android.builtInKotlin=true
android.newDsl=true
```

**`android/settings.gradle`** — Kotlin declared via the `plugins {}` block (Built-in Kotlin compatible style):
```groovy
plugins {
    id "dev.flutter.flutter-plugin-loader" version "1.0.0"
    id "com.android.application" version "8.11.1" apply false
    id "org.jetbrains.kotlin.android" version "2.2.20" apply false
}
```

## Recommended Follow-up Actions

### Short-term (Monitor `package_info_plus`)
- Watch the `plus_plugins` repository for a Built-in Kotlin migration release:
  - https://github.com/fluttercommunity/plus_plugins
  - CHANGELOG: https://pub.dev/packages/package_info_plus/changelog
- Once a KGP-free version is published, bump the version in `pubspec.yaml`.

### When a KGP-free `package_info_plus` is released
```bash
cd mobiles/sagansa
flutter pub upgrade --major-versions
flutter clean && flutter pub get
flutter build apk  # verify the warning is fully gone
```

### If Flutter forces the migration before the plugin is updated
Per the official guide, report the issue to plugin authors:
- https://docs.flutter.dev/release/breaking-changes/migrate-to-built-in-kotlin/for-app-developers#report-incompatible-kotlin-gradle-plugin-usage-to-plugin-authors

As a last resort, a Gradle init-script / dependency-substitution workaround could strip KGP, but this is **not recommended** — it risks build instability and should only be considered if Flutter hard-fails before upstream ships a fix.

